ran too long and my editor sent it back twice. Punchier. More restraint. Probably.]

Draft opening line (pick one, circle winner):
  (a) "The steam curled like a secret nobody wanted kept."
  (b) "She hadn't asked him to stay, but she hadn't asked him to leave either."
  (c) "He was, by profession, a man who noticed things — which was the whole problem."

[Margin note: (a) is doing too much. Go with (c), it's got voice.]

Research notes (for authenticity, obviously):
